|~ `::builtin`, the descriptor of a primitive, and what is declared
   under it: its constructor and its refusal, and the refusals of the
   kernel no reader reaches by a query, the table of primitives, the
   tree the evaluator does not know, the session, the printer and the
   sources of the root.
   The decisions it exists for: [D46], [D114]. ~|

:builtin
  |~~ A builtin marks a word a host implements: the value of a name
      whose code the host hands as a function, `::builtin{}`, where a
      word written in steps holds a quote.
      `::number/add | binding | /value` answers `::builtin{}`, and a
      kind the host declares builds its values by a `construct` that is
      one.

      It is a map under its tag and runs nothing by itself: a name bound
      to one reads it as data, and a call of the word runs the
      implementation its host handed.
      ::link~(::qlang/hosts | doc)
  ~~|

:builtin/isAValueOfItsOwn
  |~~ An empty descriptor is a value like any other. ~~|
  ::law~(::builtin{} | :c / | [1 2] | c | type | eq ::builtin)

:builtin/endsAPrimitive
  |~~ A primitive's value is an empty descriptor. ~~|
  ::law~(::number/add | binding | /value | eq ::builtin{})

:builtin/construct
  |~~ Reads a map as the descriptor, its fields flat under the tag. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:builtin/PayloadNotMapError
  |~~ `::builtin` holds its fields as a map, `::builtin{}` the step a
      host's verb or kind ends with; a payload of another kind is
      refused, and the descriptor is written `::builtin{}`.
  ~~|

:builtin/PayloadNotMapError/refusesAString
  |~~ A string payload is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(::builtin"hello" !| [type /actualType] | eq [::builtin/PayloadNotMapError ::string])

:builtin/PayloadNotMapError/refusesAVector
  |~~ A vector payload is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(::builtin[1 2 3] !| [type /actualType] | eq [::builtin/PayloadNotMapError ::vec])

:builtin/UnknownAstNodeTypeError
  |~~ The evaluator met a node of the parser's tree it has no rule for:
      a defect of the runtime, and no failure of the query, raised past
      the fail track to the host. The query is sound as it stands; the
      runtime is repaired, the node given its rule, and the query that
      met it is the case that shows it.
  ~~|

:builtin/AddressBoundTwiceError
  |~~ Two modules of the runtime bound an implementation under one
      address, a defect of the runtime found as it loads. Each
      implementation is bound under the address of the word or the kind
      it serves, one to an address, `number/add`.
  ~~|

:builtin/RefusalDeclaredTwiceError
  |~~ Two sites of the runtime declared one refusal under one address,
      a defect of the runtime found as it loads: the address is the tag
      the refusal answers by and the name of its page, so one site would
      speak for both. Each site declares its refusal under the address of
      what refused, the word or the part, one site to an address.
  ~~|

:builtin/RefusalFactNotDeclaredError
  |~~ A refusal of the runtime carried a fact that neither its label nor
      `::error` declares, a defect of the runtime: the facts an error
      holds are the definitions under the label that names it, and under
      `::error` for those every refusal shares. The fact is declared as a
      definition, a name, its page and the kind it holds, under the label
      of the refusal, `::proj/IndexOutOfBoundsError/length` holding
      `::number`, or under `::error` when every refusal shares it.
  ~~|

:builtin/AddressNotStringError
  |~~ A module of the runtime bound an implementation under an address
      that is no string, a defect of the runtime found as it loads. The
      address is the text of the word's address, `number/add`.
  ~~|

:builtin/ImplementationNotHandedError
  |~~ A name is `::builtin{}`, or a kind ends in one, and the host
      handed no implementation for it beside its source; `:name` names
      it, and the root is refused as it is declared. The host hands an
      implementation for the name beside the source, or writes the name
      in steps, a quote, which runs without one.
  ~~|

:builtin/TableSealedError
  |~~ The table of the language's implementations is sealed when the
      bootstrap completes, and one bound after it is refused, a defect of
      the runtime: a module of the runtime binds its implementations as
      it loads, and a host hands its own beside its sources, never to the
      table.
  ~~|

:builtin/NumberNotFiniteLeakedToPrintError
  |~~ A number of qlang is a finite double. Source cannot mint an
      infinity or a NaN — the parser refuses the literal and every
      arithmetic site answers an error of its domain — so this tag
      reports a value a host installed. The print and the JSON of the
      boundary are where such a value shows: the print would be
      `Infinity`, which no literal reads back, and JSON would write
      `null`. `:actualValue` holds the magnitude as a string, the one
      form that prints. The host keeps the numbers it hands finite, its
      bindings and the answers of its implementations, and answers an
      error of its own where its arithmetic leaves the doubles.
  ~~|

:builtin/BootstrapSourceMissingError
  |~~ A source of the language resolved to nothing, so the root lacks
      what it declares; `:uri` names the source. The host maps the source
      in the imports of its package or in the import map of a browser, or
      hands the runtime a locator of its own.
  ~~|

:builtin/RootSourceNotDeclaredError
  |~~ A source of the root answered an error, or declared again a name
      the root holds, so its declarations stay out of the root; `:uri`
      names the source and `:tagName` the refusal, for a name declared
      again `::bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError` with `:name` the name. The
      source is repaired by the page of that refusal, and a name declared
      again takes a name of its own, the root's left as they are.
  ~~|

:builtin/ImplementationNamesNoBuiltinError
  |~~ A host handed an implementation beside a source of the root for a
      name the source declares neither as a `::builtin{}` under a label
      nor as a kind ending in one; `:uri` names the source and `:name` the
      name. A verb runs its steps, a `::builtin{}` among them a step, and
      a bare name reads its value, so a host declares its primitive as a
      name under the label of its subject, `:any/fetch ::builtin{}`, the
      parts of its args names under it.
      A `::builtin{}` the host hands nothing for is refused with
      `::builtin/ImplementationNotHandedError`.
  ~~|

:builtin/SourceLoadError
  |~~ The platform resolved a `#qlang/<ns>` logical name to a path or
      URL the host could not read. The error carries `:host`
      (`:node` / `:web`), `:logicalName`, `:sourceLocation`, and either
      the underlying `:cause` or the HTTP `:status`. A host that ships
      its own catalog hands the runtime a locator of the sources of the
      language and never reaches the platform loader.
  ~~|
